From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Saurabh Jhanjee <jhanjeesaurabh@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 19:12:49 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] update: follow the latest release; exclude pre-releases

The highest tag by precedence is the wrong answer for a repository that
tags beside its releases: hermes-agent carries rc.13-v0.23.2, canary
builds and calendar tags (v2026.9.24) next to its v0.23.3 release, and
non-digit prefix stripping ranks rc.13-v0.23.2 as 13.0.0.

An input's candidates are now the tags sharing its current scheme
prefix (or matching its version_regex), without pre-releases unless
[update.inputs.<id>] prerelease = true, as in semver requirement
matching. The forge's latest release wins when it is a candidate,
read from GraphQL's latestRelease in the batch and REST
releases/latest otherwise; without releases the highest candidate
wins.
